      "text": "Day #1: kubernetes cluster architecture ",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Day #1: kubernetes cluster architecture ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "sPjJqLGGHebkGwnPQW3du",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 528.4935409119753,
      "y": 403.647467329494,
      "width": 751.9310913085938,
      "height": 244.32217958538178,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "at",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1117505001,
      "version": 176,
      "versionNonce": 521602889,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790880765799,
      "created": 1790880517677,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Control plane responsibilities:\n\n-Receive user requests\n-Store cluster state\n-Decide where applications should start\n-Detect differences between current and desired state\n-Coordinate changes across the cluster",
      "fontSize": 27.922534809757916,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Control plane responsibilities:\n\n-Receive user requests\n-Store cluster state\n-Decide where applications should start\n-Detect differences between current and desired state\n-Coordinate changes across the cluster",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "CYHU1yQB9oJe8HzN3kQ0u",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 527.4340705783148,
      "y": 701.7989987979158,
      "width": 1550.4000548251306,
      "height": 630,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "av",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1927009159,
      "version": 751,
      "versionNonce": 1291994729,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790892382474,
      "created": 1790880667572,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Control plane components\n1.API server\n- Central communication hub. Interactions with the K8s cluster must go through the API server. Internal control\nplane components communicate with each other through the API server, not directly.\n- Authentication and authorization. It validates the identity of the requester.\n\n2.etcd (key-value database)\n- Everything in the cluster, including secrets, pods, configurations, and cluster state, is stored inside etcd.\n- cluster state storage\n\n3.Controller manager\n- Monitors the cluster's actual state by querying the K8s API server\n- Compares the actual state to the user-defined state (specified in the YAML manifest)\n- If there is a difference, executes corrective actions to align the actual state with the desired state\n\n4.Scheduler\n- Assigns newly created pods to valid worker nodes.\n- choose a node for the new pod according to set of rules",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Control plane components\n1.API server\n- Central communication hub. Interactions with the K8s cluster must go through the API server. Internal control         plane components communicate with each other through the API server, not directly.\n- Authentication and authorization. It validates the identity of the requester.\n\n2.etcd (key-value database)\n- Everything in the cluster, including secrets, pods, configurations, and cluster state, is stored inside etcd.\n- cluster state storage\n\n3.Controller manager\n- Monitors the cluster's actual state by querying the K8s API server\n- Compares the actual state to the user-defined state (specified in the YAML manifest)\n- If there is a difference, executes corrective actions to align the actual state with the desired state\n\n4.Scheduler\n- Assigns newly created pods to valid worker nodes.\n- choose a node for the new pod according to set of rules",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "L99zaBlQ2FEoiEI0OZxRL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 528.5996289282751,
      "y": 1372.352332558502,
      "width": 1577.2091754480991,
      "height": 700,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aw",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1675369929,
      "version": 927,
      "versionNonce": 774856521,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790892389154,
      "created": 1790881335326,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "worker node components\n1.kubelet\n- agent(process) running on every node\n- communicate with api server on control plane\n- receive pod specifications\n- communicate with the container runtime to start the container  \n- report node and pod status to the api server\n\n2.container runtime [containerd]\n- pull container image\n- create container\n- start stop containers\n\n3.kube proxy\n- enable networking between services\n- allow trafic to reach the correct pods by configuring network rules\n\n4.pod\n- smallest deployable unit in kubernetes\n- pod can hold one container or more",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "worker node components\n1.kubelet\n- agent(process) running on every node\n- communicate with api server on control plane\n- receive pod specifications\n- communicate with the container runtime to start the container  \n- report node and pod status to the api server\n\n2.container runtime [containerd]\n- pull container image\n- create container\n- start stop containers\n\n3.kube proxy\n- enable networking between services\n- allow trafic to reach the correct pods by configuring network rules\n\n4.pod\n- smallest deployable unit in kubernetes\n- pod can hold one container or more",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8MwQUTFJsBuvbGvKarJ1G",
