    {
      "id": "-QgbgCxBGBFFUcMFpONEC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5914.121707142956,
      "y": 100.43601084868243,
      "width": 1009.5758928571421,
      "height": 1325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1P",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2100952903,
      "version": 1027,
      "versionNonce": 1267154695,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790923097091,
      "created": 1790920864123,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "abdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl apply -f deployment/deployment.yaml \ndeployment.apps/nginx-deployment created\n\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl get deployments\nNAME               READY   UP-TO-DATE   AVAILABLE   AGE\nnginx-deployment   3/3     3            3           53s\n\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl get replicasets\nNAME                          DESIRED   CURRENT   READY   AGE\nnginx-deployment-75b5f4565d   3         3         3       97s\n\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl get pods\nNAME                                READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE\nnginx-deployment-75b5f4565d-65knj   1/1     Running   0          2m19s\nnginx-deployment-75b5f4565d-8pxhh   1/1     Running   0          2m19s\nnginx-deployment-75b5f4565d-bcjh2   1/1     Running   0          2m19s\n\n#describe the deployment\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl describe deployments nginx-deployment \n\n#scaling up pods numbers \nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl scale deployment nginx-deployment --replicas=5\ndeployment.apps/nginx-deployment scaled\n\n#if i changed the deployment configurations and applied the new configurations kubectl creates a new\nreplicaset for the new version and it reaches the desired state\nand then replicaset v1 is scaled down to 0\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl rollout status deployment/nginx-deployment \ndeployment \"nginx-deployment\" successfully rolled out\n\n#notice the old replicaset is not deleted\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl get replicasets\nNAME                          DESIRED   CURRENT   READY   AGE\nnginx-deployment-75b5f4565d   0         0         0       10m\nnginx-deployment-c4f69f5d4    3         3         3       5m1s\n\n#output the deployment history in case of rollback\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl rollout history deployment/nginx-deployment \ndeployment.apps/nginx-deployment \nREVISION  CHANGE-CAUSE\n1         <none>\n2         <none>\n\n#rollback to the latest version of deployment\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl rollout undo deployment/nginx-deployment\n\n#now the old replicaset scaled up to desired state and the new one scaled to 0\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl get replicasets\nNAME                          DESIRED   CURRENT   READY   AGE\nnginx-deployment-75b5f4565d   3         3         3       15m\nnginx-deployment-c4f69f5d4    0         0         0       9m13s\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "abdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl apply -f deployment/deployment.yaml \ndeployment.apps/nginx-deployment created\n\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl get deployments\nNAME               READY   UP-TO-DATE   AVAILABLE   AGE\nnginx-deployment   3/3     3            3           53s\n\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl get replicasets\nNAME                          DESIRED   CURRENT   READY   AGE\nnginx-deployment-75b5f4565d   3         3         3       97s\n\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl get pods\nNAME                                READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE\nnginx-deployment-75b5f4565d-65knj   1/1     Running   0          2m19s\nnginx-deployment-75b5f4565d-8pxhh   1/1     Running   0          2m19s\nnginx-deployment-75b5f4565d-bcjh2   1/1     Running   0          2m19s\n\n#describe the deployment\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl describe deployments nginx-deployment \n\n#scaling up pods numbers \nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl scale deployment nginx-deployment --replicas=5\ndeployment.apps/nginx-deployment scaled\n\n#if i changed the deployment configurations and applied the new configurations kubectl creates a new replicaset for the new version and it reaches the desired state\nand then replicaset v1 is scaled down to 0\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl rollout status deployment/nginx-deployment \ndeployment \"nginx-deployment\" successfully rolled out\n\n#notice the old replicaset is not deleted\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl get replicasets\nNAME                          DESIRED   CURRENT   READY   AGE\nnginx-deployment-75b5f4565d   0         0         0       10m\nnginx-deployment-c4f69f5d4    3         3         3       5m1s\n\n#output the deployment history in case of rollback\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl rollout history deployment/nginx-deployment \ndeployment.apps/nginx-deployment \nREVISION  CHANGE-CAUSE\n1         <none>\n2         <none>\n\n#rollback to the latest version of deployment\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl rollout undo deployment/nginx-deployment\n\n#now the old replicaset scaled up to desired state and the new one scaled to 0\nabdelrahman@debian:~/k8s-series$ kubectl get replicasets\nNAME                          DESIRED   CURRENT   READY   AGE\nnginx-deployment-75b5f4565d   3         3         3       15m\nnginx-deployment-c4f69f5d4    0         0         0       9m13s\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
